[ CLIENT CPU ] <- (Instant Execution & Purge) <- [ RING 0 VIRTUAL MEMORY DRIVER ]

2.2 Core Components & Anti-Exploitation Loops

• The Remote Page-Streaming Engine (Server-Side): Slices the unswappable application memory into granular 4KB page spaces. To defeat network latency over standard Wi-Fi, it employs a Vertical Batching (Pre-fetching) Engine. When the client executes block N, the server predictively compiles blocks N+1 through N+1000 into a single encrypted network envelope.
• The Virtual Memory Bus Emulation Driver (Client-Side - Ring 0): Registers an artificial memory range within the client OS. It features an Asynchronous Page Fault Interceptor that traps hardware execution misses, absorbing the Wi-Fi transit time to prevent system watchdog timeouts or Blue Screens of Death (BSOD).
• The Volatile Memory Sanitizer (Runtime Cleaner): The absolute mitigation against REA. As the local CPU register processes execution address N, the sanitizer issues a microsecond hardware instruction to zero out or randomize execution address N-1. The AI agent is presented with a continuously moving, fragmented sequence of instructions, rendering complete control-flow graph (CFG) reconstruction mathematically impossible.

